    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0807" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">831.24/450: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-26T14:00:00-04:30">January 26, 1943—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:14 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>108. Foreign Office has inquired orally whether it is contemplated that
                    ratification instruments will be exchanged covering the Lend-Lease Agreement
                    signed at Washington, March 18, 1942<anchor n="1" xml:id="d657-f1"/> and if so,
                    whether this will be done in Caracas or at Washington. The Foreign Office
                    pointed out that the agreement itself does not mention this point.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d657-f1" n="1" xml:id="d657-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence on this agreement, see <ref target="frus1942v06#pg_735"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1942, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi>, pp. 735</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
